### Preset ID

autonomous-run-governance

### Preset Name

Autonomous Run Governance

### Version

0.2.2

### Description

Adds permission-bounded, evidence-first governance for autonomous Spec Kit delivery with validated status, stop, resume, exact-head proof, closeout, and learner guidance.

### Author

Thorsten Hindermann

### Repository URL

https://github.com/hindermath/spec-kit-preset-autonomous-run-governance

### Download URL

https://github.com/hindermath/spec-kit-preset-autonomous-run-governance/archive/refs/tags/v0.2.2.zip

### Documentation URL

https://github.com/hindermath/spec-kit-preset-autonomous-run-governance/blob/v0.2.2/README.md
  * Keeps `LocalImplementation` as the safe default and requires renewed explicit authority for `PublishPR` or `MergeAndSync`; an installed preset grants no remote permission.
  * Adds read-only status, cooperative stop, explicit resume, a validated lifecycle state, mandatory-rule drift reconciliation, and fail-closed handling of uncertain operations.
  * Retains machine-readable gate requirements and exact-head evidence, now with Bash and PowerShell validators for both lifecycle state and provider evidence.
  * Includes an extensive bilingual CEFR-B2 operating guide covering installation, delivery modes, convergence, prompts, status, stop, resume, hard-abort recovery, exact-head proof, retrospective learning, and troubleshooting.
  * Field validation includes the isolated hard-abort/resume test without a Git remote, the real randomly interrupted TuiVision Feature 030 run, and the independent Feature 031 closure. In both product runs the retrospective result was `NoPromotion`, confirming v0.2.2 without inventing a v0.2.3 release.
